{
  "id": "precalc.exp_log.log-extraneous",
  "course": "precalc",
  "topic": "exp_log",
  "kind": "equation",
  "title": "Check for extraneous roots",
  "prompt": "Solve $\\log(x) + \\log(x - 3) = 1$, where $\\log$ is the base-10 logarithm.",
  "answer_format": "All real solutions, like x = 2 or x = -3 (or {2, -3}, or 'no solution').",
  "difficulty": 2,
  "tags": [
    "logarithmic equations",
    "extraneous solutions"
  ],
  "data": {
    "equation": "log(x) + log(x - 3) = 1"
  },
  "answer": "x = 5",
  "mistakes": [],
  "hints": [
    "Combine the logs into one, then rewrite in exponential form.",
    "Plug each candidate back into the ORIGINAL equation. Logs need positive inputs."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "$\\log\\big(x(x-3)\\big) = 1 \\Rightarrow x(x-3) = 10 \\Rightarrow x^2 - 3x - 10 = 0$.",
    "$(x-5)(x+2) = 0$ gives candidates $x = 5$ and $x = -2$.",
    "$x = -2$ makes $\\log(x)$ undefined, so it's extraneous. The only solution is $x = 5$."
  ],
  "reference": {
    "book": "openstax-precalc2e",
    "section": "6.6 Exponential and Logarithmic Equations",
    "note": "Original problem."
  },
  "review": {
    "status": "draft"
  },
  "examples": [
    {
      "name": "checked the candidates",
      "submission": {
        "steps": [
          {
            "kind": "expr",
            "content": "log(x(x - 3)) = 1"
          },
          {
            "kind": "expr",
            "content": "x^2 - 3x = 10"
          },
          {
            "kind": "expr",
            "content": "(x - 5)(x + 2) = 0"
          }
        ],
        "answer": "x = 5"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": "correct"
      }
    },
